CONTEXT FROM TEXTBOOK:
This figure diagrams RNA transcription as a flat schematic of three nucleic acid strands drawn as tapered colored ribbons. A blue-violet ribbon runs across the top, labeled "DNA sense strand", marked 5' at its left tip and 3' at its right; a cyan ribbon runs along the bottom, labeled "DNA antisense strand", marked 3' at left and 5' at right. Both ribbons bow away from each other through the middle of the figure to open a bubble, and outside the bubble at each end their bases pair through vertical dot columns, C with G, A with T, and T with A at the left, G with C, A with T, and C with G at the right. Inside the bubble the sense strand's bases hang free and read T C A G C T G G C T G A A C G C G T T, while the antisense strand's exposed bases are hydrogen bonded to a magenta ribbon lying between the two, labeled "mRNA" by a leader line at its right end and marked 5' at left and 3' at right; its magenta bases read U C A G C U G G C U G A A C G C G U U. Placing the new transcript directly against its template makes the base-by-base complementarity readable in one glance, and comparing it upward with the blue-violet strand shows the two agree except that U stands wherever the sense strand carries T.

PROJECTION TYPE: axonometric
Use ordinary orthographic projection: setCameraView({ projection: 'orthographic', axisScreenAngles, heightFraction }). If the plan gives axis_screen_angles: null (a flat 2D plot/diagram), pass axisScreenAngles: null for a front-on view. Otherwise the plan does not measure per-figure angles — use a standard isometric pose: axisScreenAngles: { x: 30, z: 30 }. The source image is a PROJECTION of a 3D object: rebuild the true object — a rectangle stays a rectangle in world space — and let the camera do the projecting. Never bake the drawn parallelogram into the geometry, and never shear geometry. Omit zoom and call setCameraView after all geometry is added — the scaffold auto-fits from the projected bounding box.

ELEMENTS TO RECREATE IN 3D:
  - Blue-violet tapered ribbon (DNA sense strand) running left-to-right across the top, with arrow-notched tips at both ends
  - Cyan tapered ribbon (DNA antisense strand) running left-to-right across the bottom, with arrow-notched tips at both ends
  - S-shaped bends in both DNA ribbons that bow them apart to open the central transcription bubble
  - Magenta/pink tapered ribbon (mRNA transcript) lying in the middle of the bubble, blunt arrow tips
  - Short vertical tick stubs projecting from each ribbon representing bases (blue-violet on sense, cyan on antisense, magenta on mRNA)
  - Left flanking duplex region: three vertical dot-columns (hydrogen bonds) pairing sense C-A-T with antisense G-T-A
  - Right flanking duplex region: three vertical dot-columns pairing sense G-A-C with antisense C-T-G
  - Sense-strand letters inside the bubble: T C A G C T G G C T G A A C G C G T T (19 bases, hanging free, no pairing dots)
  - Antisense-strand letters inside the bubble: A G T C G A C C G A C T T G C G C A A (19 bases)
  - mRNA letters inside the bubble: U C A G C U G G C U G A A C G C G U U (19 magenta bases)
  - Vertical dot-columns (hydrogen bonds) between each mRNA base and the antisense base directly beneath it
  - 5' label at left tip and 3' label at right tip of the sense strand (black)
  - 3' label at left tip and 5' label at right tip of the antisense strand (black)
  - 5' label at left tip and 3' label at right tip of the mRNA (magenta)
  - Text label 'DNA sense strand' upper-left with leader arrow pointing to the sense ribbon bend
  - Text label 'DNA antisense strand' lower-left with leader arrow pointing to the antisense ribbon bend
  - Text label 'mRNA' lower-right with leader line pointing to the right end of the magenta ribbon

GEOMETRY NOTES (world-space scale, color palette, and any formula/value needed for correctness — build to these so sizes, zoom, and colors match the source; do not guess dimensions the notes already specify):
Flat 2D schematic in the XY plane, viewed front-on; no depth. World span x ∈ [-14, 14], y ∈ [-4, 4] (aspect ≈ 3.4:1, matching the very wide source). Base columns spaced 1.0 unit apart. Left flanking duplex columns at x = -12, -11, -10 (sense letters C, A, T above; antisense G, T, A below; three small vertical dots between them at y ≈ 0 spanning y = -0.45..0.45). Bubble base columns: 19 columns at x = -8.5, -7.5, ... , +9.5. Right flanking duplex columns at x = +11, +12, +13 (sense G, A, C; antisense C, T, G). Sense ribbon: thickness 0.38, centered at y = +2.55 across the bubble (x from -9.2 to +10.2), stepping down through an S-bend to y = +1.35 at the flanks (x < -9.4 and x > +10.4), ending in arrow-notched tips at x = -13.9 and +13.9. Antisense ribbon is the mirror image about y = 0: y = -2.55 in the bubble, y = -1.35 at the flanks. mRNA ribbon: thickness 0.34, straight, centered at y = +0.75, spanning x = -9.3 to +10.0 only (never enters the flanking duplexes). Base tick stubs are 0.45-long rectangles of width 0.10 pointing inward from each ribbon toward the strand it faces. Letter rows: sense bubble letters at y = +2.0 (just below the top ribbon's ticks); mRNA letters at y = +0.2 (below mRNA ribbon, magenta); antisense bubble letters at y = -0.55; hydrogen-bond dot columns (3 dots) between mRNA letters and antisense letters at y ≈ -0.15..-0.40; antisense ticks rise from the ribbon at y = -2.55 up to y ≈ -1.0. Sequences, left to right: sense bubble T C A G C T G G C T G A A C G C G T T; mRNA U C A G C U G G C U G A A C G C G U U; antisense bubble A G T C G A C C G A C T T G C G C A A. Colors: sense ribbon blue-violet #6a7fc0 at ends fading to pale #cfd8f0 at center (horizontal gradient, lightest mid-bubble); antisense ribbon cyan #23bdee at ends fading to pale #bfeafb at center; mRNA ribbon #ec2f8c at left/right ends fading to #fbd0e4 at center; ribbon ticks match their ribbon's saturated color; all DNA letters and dots black #000; all mRNA letters and its 5'/3' labels magenta #ec2f8c; annotation text black ~0.5 units tall with thin black leader arrows: 'DNA sense strand' at (-12.5, 3.6) arrow to (-9.6, 2.0); 'DNA antisense strand' at (-11.5, -3.6) arrow to (-9.0, -2.3); 'mRNA' at (11.5, -2.4) leader up-left to (9.6, 0.5). Background white.

DISCRETE CONTROLS (implement every one of these in #ui, each must work independently):
[
  {
    "id": "transcriptionPosition",
    "type": "slider",
    "teaches": "The antisense strand is the template: as the open bubble advances along the duplex, each newly exposed template base dictates one complementary ribonucleotide, and the mRNA elongates strictly 5'→3'.",
    "label": "Transcription position (bases synthesized)",
    "range": [
      0,
      19,
      1
    ],
    "default": 19
  },
  {
    "id": "pairingView",
    "type": "toggle",
    "teaches": "Which two strands are being compared changes what complementarity means: DNA–DNA uses A–T, DNA–RNA uses A–U, and the sense strand is identical to the transcript except T is replaced by U.",
    "label": "Base-pairing view",
    "options": [
      "DNA–DNA pairs",
      "DNA–RNA pairs",
      "Sense vs mRNA"
    ],
    "default": "DNA–RNA pairs"
  },
  {
    "id": "baseHover",
    "type": "hover",
    "teaches": "Each individual base has one partner and one strand polarity; hovering shows which strand is read and which base the transcript carries at that position."
  }
]

DEMO STEPS (tween through these using goToStep(); each step drives the controls above):
[
  {
    "title": "Closed duplex",
    "narration": "Before transcription the sense (blue-violet) and antisense (cyan) strands are paired end to end; note the antiparallel 5'→3' labels and the dot columns marking hydrogen bonds.",
    "state": {
      "transcriptionPosition": 0,
      "pairingView": "DNA–DNA pairs"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Bubble opens, RNA begins",
    "narration": "The strands bow apart and RNA polymerase reads the antisense strand 3'→5', laying down the first ribonucleotides: template A gives U, G gives C, T gives A.",
    "state": {
      "transcriptionPosition": 5,
      "pairingView": "DNA–RNA pairs"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Transcript elongates",
    "narration": "The bubble advances; behind it the DNA would reclose, while ahead new template bases are exposed. The magenta strand grows only at its 3' end.",
    "state": {
      "transcriptionPosition": 12,
      "pairingView": "DNA–RNA pairs"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Full transcript",
    "narration": "All 19 template bases have been read. The mRNA reads 5'-UCAGCUGGCUGAACGCGUU-3'.",
    "state": {
      "transcriptionPosition": 19,
      "pairingView": "DNA–RNA pairs"
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Sense strand vs mRNA",
    "narration": "Compare upward: the mRNA matches the sense strand base for base, except every T is replaced by U — which is why the sense strand is also called the coding strand.",
    "state": {
      "transcriptionPosition": 19,
      "pairingView": "Sense vs mRNA"
    }
  }
]

AXIS ANGLES: null — null means the source is a flat 2D figure; pass axisScreenAngles: null to setCameraView for a front-on view.

CAMERA VIEW (framing only). Call setCameraView({ projection, ...these }) AFTER all geometry is added. Keep the projection MECHANISM from PROJECTION TYPE above (orthographic / sheared-oblique / perspective). For perspective these params set the pose (azimuth/elevation/roll); for the two parallel projections pose is a standard default (see PROJECTION TYPE above), and these params set only roll and framing (heightFraction):
{
  "heightFraction": 0.55
}

NOTES: Render entirely with orthographic camera facing -Z (flat 2D); build ribbons as extruded THREE.Shape paths (rounded rect body + S-bend via quadratic curves) with vertex-colored or canvas-texture horizontal gradients to reproduce the pale-center shading. Base letters and 5'/3' labels as sprite/canvas text or troika-text so they stay crisp at this wide aspect; keep a single text atlas per color. Hydrogen-bond dots are small circle instances. For the transcription slider, clip the mRNA ribbon's right end and hide mRNA letters/ticks beyond index n, and animate the DNA bubble opening by interpolating the S-bend control points so unopened regions to the right stay paired (show their DNA-DNA dot columns) — implement bubble edges as two movable bend positions. Hover: invisible picking planes (~0.9 × 1.2 units) over each base column; on hover, dim all other columns to 25% opacity and draw a highlight box plus a small callout giving base identity, strand name, and 5'/3' direction. pairingView toggle only changes which dot columns / letter highlights are emphasized — geometry is unchanged: 'DNA–DNA' highlights the flanking dot columns, 'DNA–RNA' highlights the bubble mRNA↔antisense dots, 'Sense vs mRNA' draws faint vertical connector lines between sense and mRNA letters and outlines the T→U positions in magenta.

Follow the interaction plan above.

